/-!
# Sharpness witnesses of the even-`n` purity--spin-flip tradeoff: n = 20

GENERATED by `gen_spinflip_tradeoff_even.py`; do not edit.  Source: `spinflip_tradeoff.tex`,
`thm:purity-spinflip-tradeoff` (sharpness clause), `code/verify_spinflip_tradeoff.py` (ST-2--ST-6).

The graph is given by its neighbourhood bitmasks `adjT<n>` (bit `j` of `adjT<n> i` is set iff `i ~ j`);
`adjT<n>_symm`, `adjT<n>_irrefl`, `adjT<n>_odd` check by `decide +kernel` that it is simple and that **every vertex has
odd degree**, so that `tau (graphStateNorm Γ) = 1` (`tau_gsn_eq_one`).  `rankSumT<n>` is the kernel-checked sum
`Σ_{|S| = k} 2^{k - rk_2 Γ[S,S^c]}` (over one representative of each orbit of the dihedral automorphism group,
weighted by the orbit size: `sum_cuts_reps`, `NQubit/Graph/Symmetry.lean`; `symQ<n>` lists the group, `symR<n>` the
representatives with their orbit sizes), and `meanRdmPurity_graphT<n>` the resulting `π_k = L_n + c_n`.
Claim class: exact finite certificate (`decide +kernel`).
-/

@[expose] public section

